Spec: Domain

Purpose:
  Pure, deterministic logic every screen relies on: distances, ride stats, time bounds, formatters,
    route progress and route following. Built test-first with EXACT.

Structure:
  ./activity_type.dart: Activity types and their stored ids
  ./distance_calculator.dart: Haversine distance seam
  ./ride_stats.dart: Per-ride duration, distance and speeds
  ./stats_aggregation.dart: Week, day and year totals
  ./time_bounds.dart: Local day, week and year bounds
  ./formatters.dart: Duration, date and distance formatting
  ./ride_title.dart: Display title of a ride
  ./max_speed.dart: Live top speed
  ./fallback_speed.dart: Display speed when GPS reports none
  ./heading.dart: Heading-up bearing and route-tail split
  ./live_activity_snapshot.dart: iOS Live Activity content and push timing
  ./countdown_cue.dart: Seconds the countdown announces
  ./route_markers.dart: Start, finish or loop endpoint markers
  ./route_progress.dart: Projection of a position onto a reference route
  ./follow_tracker.dart: Following a route in either direction, with its helpers in `follow_*.dart`
  ./route_group.dart: Original plus follows, best time
  ./route_row_stats.dart: One comparison-sheet row
  ./route_selection.dart: Followed-routes search and summary

Owns:
  /test/domain/domain_test_helpers.dart

References:
  /docs/specs/history/04-domain.md

Must:
  Domain code imports only `dart:*`, `intl` and the Drift row types.
  Time-dependent functions take an injectable `nowMs`.
  Thresholds and limits are named constants.

Forbids:
  `package:flutter`
  Riverpod, database access, platform channels and network access

Done when:
  Every `Scenario` and `Example` of the governing spec has a test.
